"TCPL delivered a resilient but uninspiring FY26 — consolidated revenue ~INR 1,836 cr (+3% YoY) with EBITDA margin holding ~17.3% — as steady domestic volume growth (ahead of consumer-market growth) offset export weakness from Middle East shipping disruption; the headline pinch was below EBITDA, where an INR 18 cr MTM on the EUR ECB and a high deferred-tax (capex-driven timing) charge compressed EPS to an unusually low level for TCPL's history. The structural story is intact: 26th straight dividend year (INR 25/share), Chennai (>50% utilized) and Silvassa gravure ramping, a 4th flexible line by end-FY27, but management is deliberately calibrating FY27 capex down to ~INR 100 cr amid RM (paperboard) inflation and geopolitical uncertainty.","trig":[]},"lm":"","m":3732,"mem":0,"pdd":"","prev_stage":1,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"r":null,"s":"TCPLPACK","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"3214.0","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"7.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"0.8","vpe_zone_cumul_df":""},"t":"basing"}},"s":"TCPLPACK"}